ra89r_re
========

Firmware reverse engineering and a custom firmware for the Retevis RA89R /
RA89G (TYT UV8800 / TH9000D family, Puya PY32F403).  See AGENTS.md.

This product includes software developed as part of the
UV-K1/K5V3 custom firmware project
(https://github.com/armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom, based on
https://github.com/DualTachyon/uv-k5-firmware), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).  Those files keep their original
copyright headers, and this list is where each imported file is recorded
progressively, as the RA89R port brings them in.

Imported from the UV-K1/K5V3 project
------------------------------------

| file | state | adaptation |
|---|---|---|
| `firmware/App/driver/bk4819.c` `.h` `bk4819-regs.h` | on `develop`, validated on the radio | transport is `rf_bus.c` (chip select `PB8`); local delay; two audio-path calls go through a registered callback; the four `gEeprom` reads became driver-local setters |
| `firmware/App/font.c` `font.h` | verbatim | none -- font tables (`gFontBig`, `gFontBigDigits`, `gFontSmall`, `gFont3x5`, `gFontSmallBold`) |
| `firmware/App/bitmaps.c` `bitmaps.h` | verbatim | none -- icon bitmaps |
| `firmware/App/driver/st7565.c` `.h` | adapted | same API and layout as the K1 (`gStatusLine[128]`, `gFrameBuffer[7][128]`, status line = page 0, frame lines = pages 1..7, `+4` column offset in `DrawLine`); the transport is this repo's bit-banged `driver/lcd_st7565.c` instead of the K1's hardware SPI, and the init is the bootloader-proven sequence |

Feature macros for the imported files live in `firmware/App/port_features.h` and
are force-included by the build (`-include`), so the imported sources stay
byte-comparable with upstream.
